   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "How's it going?",
     "texto": [
      "**Wie geht's?** is the short form of **Wie geht es dir?** (how are you?). With «Sie» (formal): **Wie geht es Ihnen?**",
      "You answer **Gut, danke** (good, thanks) or **Sehr gut** (very good). Other answers: **Es geht** (so-so), **Nicht so gut** (not so good).",
      "To ask it back: **Und dir?** or **Und Ihnen?**"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Introducing someone",
     "texto": [
      "**Das ist Paul** (this is Paul). «Das ist» works for men, women and things.",
      "**Er** means «he» and **sie** (lowercase) means «she».",
      "In German the subject is **required**: you cannot say just «ist müde». You have to say **Er ist müde** (he is tired)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
